                            <h2 class="title" id="overview_heading">Overview</h2>
                            <p>As part of its new Climate Action Program, Mt. San Antonio College (Mt. SAC) had developed a wide variety of courses designed to prepare students for careers in sustainability. The college reached out to us to help create an explainer video that would get students and faculty excited about the new opportunities.</p>
<p>Eager to help Mt. SAC promote its innovative new programs, we got to work.</p>
                        
                        

                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_understand_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="1">Understand</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>The Mt. SAC team wanted the video to explain the concept of sustainability to students, before diving into the course offerings available through the college. In particular, the Mt. SAC team wanted students to understand that sustainability is about more than just recycling and renewable energy.</p>
<p>Accordingly, we spent time researching the topic of sustainability, and outlined an approach to the video that would cover key concepts such as the UN’s Pillars of Sustainability (People, Planet, and Prosperity) and the 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) identified in 2015.</p>
<p><img src="/hs-fs/hubfs/planet.f06506d4.png" alt="planet" width="909" height="474" loading="lazy" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 909px;" srcset="/hs-fs/hubfs/planet.d5a3a683.png 455w, /hs-fs/hubfs/planet.f06506d4.png 909w, /hs-fs/hubfs/planet.720d10d5.png 1364w, /hs-fs/hubfs/planet.d00fe504.png 1818w, /hs-fs/hubfs/planet.5def82ef.png 2273w, /hs-fs/hubfs/planet.6ec1330a.png 2727w" sizes="(max-width: 909px) 100vw, 909px"></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_explore_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading align-right" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="2">Explore</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>Working side by side with Mt. SAC team members, we developed a script that defined the core concept of sustainability, explored career opportunities in this growing field, and highlighted sustainability-related course offerings and other resources available to Mt. SAC students.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Through several rounds of revision, we arrived at a script that clearly communicates a great deal of vital information in a short amount of time, and offers compelling calls to action for students interested in learning more about sustainability at Mt. SAC and beyond.</p>
<p><img src="/hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.7c2add40.png" alt="wide variety of opportunities" width="910" height="509" loading="lazy" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 910px;" srcset="/hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.0ea894fa.png 455w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.7c2add40.png 910w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.92cfd8b5.png 1365w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.a74675a4.png 1820w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.88711afb.png 2275w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wide-variety-of-opportunities.1bbbca4e.png 2730w" sizes="(max-width: 910px) 100vw, 910px"></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_create_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="3">Create</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>Script in hand, we were ready to begin production.</p>
<p>We led the Mt. SAC team through the process of selecting a voiceover artist, and directed a successful recording session. Over the course of several weeks, we then presented Mt. SAC with several storyboard options; guided the team through the animation process; and finally presented both raw and subtitled versions of the final video files.</p>
<p><img src="/hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.dfdd07b2.png" alt="wall sitting" width="918" height="475" loading="lazy" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 918px;" srcset="/hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.7cbbd982.png 459w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.dfdd07b2.png 918w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.9b4249fa.png 1377w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.9e404b91.png 1836w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.6ff86f76.png 2295w, /hs-fs/hubfs/wall-sitting.d89eee65.png 2754w" sizes="(max-width: 918px) 100vw, 918px"></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_launch_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading align-right" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="4">Launch</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>The Mt. SAC team is happy with the final product, and eager to share the video with students and fellow faculty members.</p>
<p>We’ve been honored to help Mt. SAC promote its sustainability initiatives on and off campus, and we look forward to working together again in the future.</p>
